Builtin cast targets include eleven fixed numeric types:

- `I8`, `I16`, `I32`, `I64`
- `U8`, `U16`, `U32`, `U64`
- `F16`, `F32`, `F64`

`Byte`, `Dec` and `Dec0` through `Dec256` remain separate targets. `Bool`,
`String`, `Char` and `Error` also have builtin conversion policies.

Same-type casts are invalid. `Byte` remains distinct from `U8`, and no cast
silently changes one into the other.

The target comes from an immediate typed destination such as an annotation,
return slot, concrete parameter, field or typed collection entry. An
unresolved generic slot and a distant later use cannot supply it.

Not every source-target pair can convert. Numeric pairs follow their complete
types, not a value the compiler happens to know. See @./#cast-targets (Cast
targets) for exactness, rounding and failure rules.
